    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mullery O’Gara are proud to present 12 St. Peters Road to the open market. A wonderful 3 bedroom plus attic room family home, well set back from the road with ample off street parking, south facing garden, garage and rear pedestrian and vehicular access.\r\n\r\nThis wonderful home has been extremely well maintained by the current owners and is presented in immaculate condition throughout. With generously proportioned and light filled accommodation throughout.  \r\n\r\nBriefly comprising of entrance hallway with understairs storage off. There are two fine sized interconnecting reception rooms with large window to the front and double doors leading to the garden to the rear. To the front is the living with solid wood floor and open fire with pine mantpiece, the lounge/dining is to the rear. Beyond the hallway is the kitchen/breakfastroom, upgraded in recent years with a range of kitchen units, sink unit and door to rear lobby. Off the lobby is a utility area plumbed for the washing machine, door to garden and access to a downstairs shower room. \r\n\r\nUpstairs the room proportions are equally as impressive, bedroom 1 is to the front with built in wardrobes.. Bedroom 2 is to the rear of the property with built in wardrobes and bedroom 3 is to the front with built in wardrobes. There is a family bathroom at first floor level which is fully tiled with bath, shower attachment, w.c and vanity whb.  \r\n\r\nOff the landing are stairs to the attic room with dormer window and ample storage in the eaves. \r\n\r\nOutside to the front is low maintenance garden with off street parking for a number of cars. To the rear is a wonderful low maintenance garden with a southerly aspect laid out in a paved patio area, decked area and bedding. Additionally there is a timber shed for storage and garage. The spacious garage has electricity and rear vehicular access. \r\n\r\nSt. Peter’s Road is positioned in a much sought after and established residential location beside an excellent choice of primary and secondary schools within the locality, excellent recreational and leisure facilities found in Tymon Park, St Mary's Rugby Club, St. Jude’s GAA Club. This area is within a short distance to Lidl on the Greenhills Road, Ashleaf shopping centre and Super Valu Walkinstown. The property is convenient to the city centre and M50 with numerous bus routes in the area giving access into the city and beyond."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall \r\nSolid wood floor and understairs storage. \r\n\r\nLivingroom\r\nSolid wood flooring, recessed lights, ceiling coving, open fire with pine mantle and double doors to \r\n\r\nLounge \r\nSolid wood flooring, recessed lights, ceiling coving and double doors to garden\r\n\r\nKitchen / Breakfast room \r\nLaminate floor, recessed lights, 1 1/3 sink unit, extractor fan, plumbed for washing machine and door to lobby \r\n\r\nLobby \r\nPlumbed for washing machine, laminate floor and door to garden. \r\n\r\nShower room \r\nShower, w.c, vanity whb with storage, recessed lights, tiled floor and walls\r\n\r\nFirst floor \r\nBedroom 1 (Front)\r\nBuilt in wardrobes and laminate floor. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (Rear)\r\nBuilt in wardrobes and laminate floor. \r\n\r\nBedroom 3 (Front)\r\nBuilt in wardrobes and laminate floor.\r\n\r\nBathroom \r\nBath with shower attachment, w.c, vanity whb with storage, recessed shelf, recessed lights, tiled floor and walls \r\n\r\nLanding \r\nStairs to \r\n\r\nAttic room \r\nDormer window, solid wood flooring, recessed lights and eaves storage. \r\n\r\nOutside\r\nAmple off street parking to the front. \r\nLow maintenance south facing garden to rear with decked and paved areas. Timber shed and rear pedestrian access. \r\n\r\nGarage \r\nElectricity, vehicular access."
